    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. but when people talk about the \"success\" of that era in most textbooks, they usually focus on how it basically saved the economy from the stagnation of the 70s. in your research, do you see that being treated as the primary takeaway, or is the inequality/instability stuff given equal weight in the actual consensus?",
