      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Textbooks often frame the 1980s shift primarily as a successful break from the \"stagflation\" of the 1970s, emphasizing renewed growth and lower inflation. However, more nuanced academic research gives significant weight to the rising concerns over income disparity and greater systemic risk. While the recovery narrative is prominent in introductory texts, advanced literature strongly emphasizes that the growth came at a substantial cost to economic equity and stability.",
      "source": "target",
