      "role": "user",
      "content": "got it. so if i'm writing this paper, would it be accurate to say that the consensus among most economists is that deregulation was fundamentally a net positive for innovation and long term growth, even if it had some messy social consequences? like, is the 'growth' side considered the established reality and the other stuff just the critique?",
